WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.985 --> 00:00:14.826
knew my parents were still out there!"

2
00:00:15.186 --> 00:00:15.926
Zann exclaimed.

3
00:00:15.946 --> 00:00:18.547
"They must have found World X."

4
00:00:19.508 --> 00:00:23.470
"Yeah. Too bad we still don't know how to get there," Perda said.

5
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.331
Darb looked thoughtful.

6
00:00:25.351 --> 00:00:27.972
"We know World X has a blue sky.

7
00:00:29.032 --> 00:00:34.415
If we peek through the wormholes and check every world with blue skies, we'll find World X eventually."

8
00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.716
Zann smiled hopefully.

9
00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:37.977
"That could work!"

10
00:00:39.218 --> 00:00:42.239
"There are lots of worlds with blue skies though."

11
00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:44.901
Gliss glanced up at the Paxian sky.

12
00:00:44.921 --> 00:00:50.984
"Yeah. Including that creepy no-magic world we got stuck in," Perda said.

13
00:00:51.004 --> 00:00:53.625
"We'll be careful," Zann said.

14
00:00:53.645 --> 00:00:58.488
"We'll hang onto the edge of each wormhole so it can't close behind us.

15
00:00:59.428 --> 00:01:05.050
If we recognize that no-magic world, we can duck back into the vortex before we're trapped."

16
00:01:06.291 --> 00:01:09.672
"Like we did the second time in Fardark," Perda said with a nod.

17
00:01:09.692 --> 00:01:11.393
"I guess that could work."

18
00:01:12.493 --> 00:01:14.034
Vee was listening carefully.

19
00:01:14.054 --> 00:01:18.436
"If you find Morb, will you look for our stolen mibbit?"

20
00:01:18.676 --> 00:01:19.176
she asked.

21
00:01:20.017 --> 00:01:21.437
"We're very worried about it."

22
00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:23.458
"Sure," Darb said.

23
00:01:23.478 --> 00:01:24.959
"What do mibbits look like?"

24
00:01:25.859 --> 00:01:26.579
"I'll show you."

25
00:01:26.999 --> 00:01:28.140
Vee closed her eyes.

26
00:01:29.072 --> 00:01:32.314
Soon a small, fluffy creature hopped out of the forest.

27
00:01:33.514 --> 00:01:35.195
Zing let out an excited chirp.

28
00:01:35.215 --> 00:01:38.897
"Not so fast," Zann said, grabbing the dragon.

29
00:01:38.917 --> 00:01:43.080
"That little critter is definitely not lunch."

30
00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.723
"It doesn't look very scary," Perda commented as the mibbit nibbled at the grass.

31
00:01:49.743 --> 00:01:50.544
Vee smiled.

32
00:01:50.984 --> 00:01:51.364
"I know.

33
00:01:51.884 --> 00:01:55.166
But trust me—you don't want to panic one."

34
00:01:55.186 --> 00:01:58.808
"How can we rescue the stolen one without panicking it?"

35
00:01:58.988 --> 00:01:59.609
Darb asked.

36
00:02:00.709 --> 00:02:01.870
Vee picked up the mibbit.

37
00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:03.471
It snuggled into her arms.

38
00:02:03.491 --> 00:02:08.695
"If the mibbit panics, you can calm it by rubbing its ears."

39
00:02:09.656 --> 00:02:12.858
She demonstrated, and the mibbit let out a squeak of pleasure.

40
00:02:13.698 --> 00:02:15.139
Darb was watching intently.

41
00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.100
"May I try?"

42
00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.962
"Certainly." Vee held out the mibbit.

43
00:02:19.903 --> 00:02:22.224
"Easy, little fellow," Darb cooed.

44
00:02:23.225 --> 00:02:25.146
He rubbed the mibbit's long ears.

45
00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.088
Vee smiled.

46
00:02:27.404 --> 00:02:30.787
"The soothing effects usually last a couple of hours."

47
00:02:31.668 --> 00:02:32.648
Perda looked impatient.

48
00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:33.889
"Let's get going.

49
00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:37.072
The sooner we warn someone about Morb, the better."

50
00:02:37.092 --> 00:02:40.355
"Right." Zann took a step toward the lake.

51
00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:42.617
"Guess it's time to get wet again."

52
00:02:42.637 --> 00:02:44.939
"There's no need for that."

53
00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:48.802
Vee set down the mibbit, which hopped away into the forest.

54
00:02:48.822 --> 00:02:51.084
"I can take you there by boat."

55
00:02:54.516 --> 00:02:57.638
Minutes later Zann and his friends were back in the vortex.

56
00:02:57.658 --> 00:03:00.540
"Pax was nice," Gliss said.

57
00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.122
"I wouldn't mind visiting again someday."

58
00:03:03.142 --> 00:03:05.343
"Yeah." Perda laughed.

59
00:03:05.363 --> 00:03:08.165
"Just watch out for those scary mibbits!"

60
00:03:09.246 --> 00:03:10.527
Zann was barely listening.

61
00:03:11.427 --> 00:03:14.109
He watched for glimpses of blue through the wormholes.

62
00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:20.434
The first world they passed showed a drab green sky, and the next two skies were gray.

63
00:03:21.594 --> 00:03:23.736
Then he spotted a flash of blue.

64
00:03:24.672 --> 00:03:25.273
"There's one!"

65
00:03:25.453 --> 00:03:25.853
he cried.

66
00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:31.298
He was so excited that he pulled himself all the way through the wormhole, flopping on his stomach

67
00:03:31.338 --> 00:03:32.118
on the other side.

68
00:03:32.138 --> 00:03:36.022
"Oof!" Darb grunted as he landed beside Zann.

69
00:03:36.042 --> 00:03:39.345
"Hey," Perda complained, sitting up.

70
00:03:39.365 --> 00:03:43.388
"You were supposed to hold onto the edge, remember?"

71
00:03:44.949 --> 00:03:46.110
Zann's face flushed.

72
00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:51.235
"Sorry," he mumbled, glancing back at the wormhole as it swirled shut.

73
00:03:51.255 --> 00:03:52.676
"I forgot."

74
00:03:53.408 --> 00:03:54.749
"Um, guys?"

75
00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:55.590
Darb said.

76
00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.231
"We're not alone."

77
00:03:58.312 --> 00:04:01.995
Five girls stood in a semicircle, staring at the visitors.

78
00:04:02.916 --> 00:04:04.897
All of them were Zann's age or younger.

79
00:04:05.738 --> 00:04:11.703
They looked almost like regular Magicians, except for their green skin and vine-like hair.

80
00:04:11.723 --> 00:04:14.045
"What are they?"

81
00:04:14.505 --> 00:04:15.946
one of the girls whispered to the others.

82
00:04:16.847 --> 00:04:17.968
Zann climbed to his feet.

83
00:04:17.988 --> 00:04:20.630
"Hey. What world is this?"

84
00:04:21.611 --> 00:04:22.912
The girls all stared at him.

85
00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:24.701
"It speaks!"

86
00:04:25.181 --> 00:04:25.741
one of them said.

87
00:04:26.721 --> 00:04:28.022
Another girl noticed Zing.

88
00:04:28.042 --> 00:04:29.763
"Look, a dragon!"

89
00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:30.923
She let out a whistle.

90
00:04:31.723 --> 00:04:35.565
Zing chirped with delight and scampered over, snuggling against her leg.

91
00:04:36.746 --> 00:04:37.686
Zann was surprised.

92
00:04:38.406 --> 00:04:41.087
Zing didn't usually warm up to strangers so quickly.

93
00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.929
Zann glanced at Darb, who shrugged.

94
00:04:44.849 --> 00:04:47.430
One of the girls turned to address Gliss and Perda.

95
00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:50.852
"What sort of odd creatures are you traveling with?"

96
00:04:51.152 --> 00:04:51.632
she asked.

97
00:04:52.544 --> 00:04:53.505
"You mean Zing?"

98
00:04:53.685 --> 00:04:54.185
Perda said.

99
00:04:54.205 --> 00:04:56.027
"He's a fire whistler."

100
00:04:56.727 --> 00:04:59.149
Hearing his name, Zing let out another chirp.

101
00:04:59.169 --> 00:05:03.592
"Not the dragon, silly," the tallest girl said, laughing.

102
00:05:03.612 --> 00:05:06.694
"We mean those creatures."

103
00:05:07.195 --> 00:05:08.716
She pointed at the two boys.

104
00:05:08.736 --> 00:05:10.857
"Zann and Darb?"

105
00:05:11.118 --> 00:05:12.278
Gliss said uncertainly.

106
00:05:12.298 --> 00:05:13.599
"What do you mean?"

107
00:05:13.619 --> 00:05:15.941
"They're so odd!"

108
00:05:16.201 --> 00:05:16.862
the girl said.

109
00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:19.263
"We've never seen anything like them!

110
00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.241
Are they dolls, made to look almost human?"

111
00:05:23.261 --> 00:05:26.262
"Or perhaps some magical apparition?"

112
00:05:26.502 --> 00:05:27.682
Another girl looked excited.

113
00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:30.283
"We've heard tales of such things!"

114
00:05:30.303 --> 00:05:34.344
"We're not dolls or apparitions," Zann said.

115
00:05:35.164 --> 00:05:36.885
All the girls giggled and stared.

116
00:05:36.905 --> 00:05:40.506
"It speaks almost as if it understands us!"

117
00:05:40.946 --> 00:05:41.546
one exclaimed.

118
00:05:42.326 --> 00:05:43.326
Gliss shook her head.

119
00:05:43.346 --> 00:05:44.967
"I don't understand.

120
00:05:45.527 --> 00:05:46.727
They're just boys."

121
00:05:46.747 --> 00:05:50.085
"Boys?" The oldest girl echoed.

122
00:05:50.105 --> 00:05:53.347
"Is this a species related to humans?"

123
00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:57.929
"Wow, you've really never seen boys before?"

124
00:05:58.209 --> 00:05:59.630
Perda sounded amazed.

125
00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:01.151
"How can that be?"

126
00:06:01.171 --> 00:06:03.633
"Never mind," Zann said.

127
00:06:03.653 --> 00:06:05.334
"We're wasting time."

128
00:06:06.214 --> 00:06:08.435
He glanced at the spot where the wormhole had been.

129
00:06:08.455 --> 00:06:10.477
"Is there magic in this world?"

130
00:06:11.317 --> 00:06:13.858
The girls stared at him in wonder, not responding.

131
00:06:14.719 --> 00:06:16.140
Perda repeated Zann's question.

132
00:06:17.024 --> 00:06:19.905
"Of course there's magic here," one of the girls told her.

133
00:06:21.105 --> 00:06:23.646
Next Zann asked about Wyssa and Morb.

134
00:06:24.666 --> 00:06:26.567
Once again the girls merely stared.

135
00:06:27.427 --> 00:06:30.388
But when Gliss repeated the question, the girls shook their heads.

136
00:06:30.408 --> 00:06:34.849
"You're the first visitors in many moons," one said.

137
00:06:34.869 --> 00:06:39.070
"Okay." Zann was already tired of the strange girls.

138
00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:40.610
"Then let's get going."

139
00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:42.671
"Did you hear what it said?"

140
00:06:42.931 --> 00:06:43.671
a girl exclaimed.

141
00:06:44.592 --> 00:06:45.952
"Yes. I'll fix it."

142
00:06:46.708 --> 00:06:49.949
The oldest girl let out a puff of air toward Zann and Darb.

143
00:06:51.049 --> 00:06:54.190
Suddenly the two boys were completely immobilized!

144
00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:58.651
"Hey!" Zann cried—or tried to anyway.

145
00:06:59.131 --> 00:07:00.392
He could barely move his lips.

146
00:07:01.372 --> 00:07:02.732
"What did you do to them?"

147
00:07:02.913 --> 00:07:03.613
Perda demanded.

148
00:07:04.433 --> 00:07:05.313
The girls giggled.

149
00:07:05.713 --> 00:07:07.214
"They're fine," one said.

150
00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:09.414
"Yes," another said.

151
00:07:09.434 --> 00:07:12.395
"We don't want them to run off just yet, that's all.

152
00:07:13.335 --> 00:07:15.176
First we must show them to Mother!"
